# Your own settings, kept out of the repo.
#
# config.yaml and state/ are both ignored here and both have to be committed
# on a fork that uses the GitHub Actions path: a fresh runner has no memory,
# so an uncommitted config is a config it cannot see. `git add -f` them there.
# That is one deliberate flag, against a file that is otherwise impossible to
# commit by accident.
#
# config.yaml was tracked until 2026-08-25, which meant `job-radar setup` on a
# fresh clone reported "Wrote config.yaml" and `git status` reported a
# modified tracked file. Every later pull conflicted. Untracking it was not
# enough on its own: an untracked file that is not ignored is one `git add -A`
# away from being tracked again, which is exactly what happened within the
# hour, so it is ignored as well.
#
# If you want a private config even on a public fork, put it in
# config.local.yaml, which the CLI prefers over config.yaml.
config.yaml
config.local.yaml
*.local.yaml

# Scan output. Regenerated every run; publish it via Pages rather than commits.
out/

# Maintainer working files. The harvester lives in a separate private repo;
# these are what it leaves behind if it is run from here.
harvest/
raw/
*.checkpoint.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Your scan history. NOT ignored for forks that use the Actions path, which
# have to commit it: see the note in the README. It is ignored here because
# this is the upstream repo and the maintainer's own search history has no
# business being in it.
state/

# Generated design previews. These embed real scan results, so they must not
# be committed to a public repo. The generators next to them are source.
design/*.html

# Your application history. Personal, and not the tool's business.
applications.local.yaml

# The database. Holds your application history and document paths.
data/
*.db
.backups/

# Raw output from tools/probe_rate_limit.py. 571 requests of headers and
# statuses, and the conclusions drawn from it live in tests/test_rate_model.py
# and docs/PLATFORMS.md, which is where a reader will look. The log is the
# working, not the finding.
tools/rate_probe_log.jsonl

# A downloaded or locally built shard set. Tens of megabytes of somebody
# else and regenerable from `job-radar seed build`, so it has no business in
# anybody history.
seed/
seed-build/
seed-build.new/
.seed-cache/

# Local scan logs. Run output, not source, and it names the boards you scan.
logs/
